# OS/7 desktop (GNOME).
#
# Present in the LIVE image on every architecture, because:
#   a) Calamares is a Qt GUI application and needs a running desktop session to
#      run the install at all, and
#   b) GUI vs. headless is an INSTALLER-TIME choice (README) - the installer
#      removes the desktop for a headless install rather than the ISO shipping
#      two package bases.
#
# GNOME specifically is required for supported Microsoft Intune enrollment.
#
# NOTE: this list contains no Microsoft packages. The Microsoft APT repos do not
# exist yet during the package-list pass - they are added by hook 0010, so
# anything from them must be installed in a later hook.
# (docs/BUILD-NOTES.md #10)

ubuntu-desktop-minimal
gnome-shell
gdm3
nautilus
gnome-terminal

# --- Installer ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Calamares 3.3.14 in resolute ships the zfs and zfshostid modules, which is why
# the README's Calamares decision is viable. Configuration is still to be
# written - see installer/README.md.
calamares

# The "familiar feel" extensions (dash-to-panel taskbar, ArcMenu start menu) are
# deliberately absent: neither has a GNOME-50-compatible build in the resolute
# archive. Hook 0070 logs this gap rather than failing the build.
